        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The new UI feels more geared to being used on mobile devices than for actually being used on a vr headset. I do not understand the approach that the designers went for with this.\n\nAnyone attempting to use this with unsteady/disabled hands without some sort of eye-tracking setup in it's place is bound to have issues compared to the legacy menu.\n\nThe new menu also expects everyone to know what old icons mean without ever having played VRC before, I know it shows their function at the bottom of the screen but that can be potentially cut off based on display position.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-02T08:49:44.432Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "(This is related to the \"Quick Menu Refresh\" in build 1319, but also includes mention of fundamental UI/UX issues, such as MM settings, etc.)\n\nThe UI with common style buttons is simpler, but it is much less understandable than the icon-based settings UI.\n\nThe current QM settings UI requires interpreting items described in mostly text, and it is not easy to predict what options are available for given settings or what effect a setting change will have. Definitely, the QM settings operation is more non-intuitive than before.\n\nIn addition, the change from several icons to one setting per line has reduced the number of settings per screen, and some low-priority items are now displayed at the top, requiring scrolling to access major settings, which is very inconvenient.\n\nAlso, the current QM Settings UI is part of the MM settings, not **Quick**.\n\nFYI, I have also written [Canny about Quest's hand tracking operation setting](https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/1292-finger-track-locomotion-setting-choices-are-confusing) with similar intentions. \n\nBoth have in common that the icons are gone and have become non-intuitive.\n\nThe UI does not have to be the same as before, but I would like VRChat to see a properly designed UI that is more **quickly and easily understandable**.\n\n[JP]\n\n(これはビルド1319の\"Quick Menu Refresh\"に関連する話ですが、MM設定などを含んだ根本的なUI/UXの問題についての言及も含みます。)\n\n共通のボタンを使ったUIは簡素ですが、アイコンを活用した設定UIと比較すると理解しやすさを大きく損ないます。\n\n現在のQM設定UIでは、殆どが文字だけで記述されている項目を読み解く必要があり、その設定にどのような選択肢があるのか、設定変更がどのような効果をもたらすのかを予測するのは容易ではありません。明らかに、以前よりQMの設定操作が非直感的になっています。\n\nまた、アイコンで並んでいた設定項目が1行に1項目ずつに変わったことで1画面辺りの設定項目数が減ったほか、優先度の低い幾つかの項目が上部に表示され、主要な設定へのアクセスにスクロールが必要になったりしており、これは非常に不便です。\n\n加えて、このQM設定UIはMM設定の一部であって、\"Quick\"とは言えません。\n\n参考までに、Questのハンドトラッキングでの操作設定について似たような意図のCanny( https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/1292-finger-track-locomotion-setting-choices-are-confusing )を書いたこともあります。どちらも、アイコンが無くなって非直感的になってしまったというポイントが共通しています。\n\n以前と同じUIである必要はありませんが、適切にデザインされた、より\"即座に理解出来る\"UIにしていただきたいです。",
